      "floor": {
        "amount": 1800,
        "appliesTo": "Basic monthly salary, Singapore production and operator roles",
        "source": "JTE, November 2026",
        "short": "The basic salary is only half the story. Aim for a gross salary around S$3,000.",
        "long": "Production jobs pay a lower basic salary than most industries, with overtime and incentives making up the rest. S$1,800 basic is about the lowest anyone will accept. S$2,000 is normal. S$2,200 to S$2,500 gets you noticeably better people. But the number they look at is the gross salary, and around S$3,000 is what wins them. Fewer people want a lot of overtime now, so a package that only works with heavy OT is hard to sell.",
        "displayAmount": 3000
      },
      "note": "The basic salary is only half the picture here. How simple or complex the job is affects the salary as much as the level does. At the bottom of the range, fewer people apply and hiring takes longer."
